  "production_date": "probably 1500-10",
  "brief_description": "Christ carries the Cross on which he will be crucified to Golgotha, the site of his execution (John 19: 17). He is surrounded by soldiers and guards who goad him on his way as he struggles under the weight of the Cross. His body is doubled over and large teardrops fall down his face.  The thorns plaited around his head to form a makeshift crown have cut his forehead, which is red with blood. Two of the guards hold him by a rope which is tied around his waist.\n\nThe painting may have been part of a series of images showing the Passion of Christ (the name for the events including his arrest, torture and death). It was once thought to have been painted by a Westphalian artist, but is now regarded as reflecting the work of painters in Lübeck in North Germany.",
